    <p class="tiny muted">The M40 and MI50 are eBay legends: enormous VRAM, tiny price, big cooling energy. Arc is the value newcomer. 🔥</p>
    <aside class="notes">This is the crowd-pleaser. The M40 needs a 3D-printed shroud and a blower fan. The MI50 has 32GB of HBM2 for peanuts but ROCm will test your patience. The 16GB gaming cards are the sane middle path.</aside>
</section>

<!-- HARDWARE - the M40 / MI50 detail -->
<section>
    <section data-background-color="#1a0a2e">
        <h3>🟩 Tesla M40 24GB - The Cursed Champion</h3>
        <ul class="spacious">
            <li>24 GB VRAM for the price of a nice dinner 🍽️</li>
            <li>Passive cooling = you MUST bolt on a blower fan 🌬️</li>
            <li>Maxwell era: slow-ish, no modern tensor cores</li>
            <li>Runs 14B models happily via llama.cpp / Ollama ✅</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted">Perfect for a homelab "AI box" that idles quietly in a closet.</p>
        <aside class="notes">The M40 is a meme-tier card. It works! Just accept the cooling jank and modest speed. Great for batch/chat where latency is forgiving.</aside>
    </section>

    <section data-background-color="#2a1a1a">
        <h3>🟥 MI50 32GB - The HBM2 Sleeper</h3>
        <ul class="spacious">
            <li>32 GB of fast HBM2 bandwidth 🚀</li>
            <li>ROCm or Vulkan backend in llama.cpp</li>
            <li>Fits bigger models or big context windows 📚</li>
            <li>Driver setup is the boss fight 🐉</li>
        </ul>
        <aside class="notes">The MI50 is the sleeper pick if you can survive the ROCm install. 32GB opens up 14B at higher precision or long contexts.</aside>
    </section>
</section>

